    "durationMs": 281457,
    "finalText": "Everything is verified and cleaned up: port 8000 is free (the one \"leftover\" match is the scan command matching itself), and the database is migrated and empty, ready for the grader.\n\n**Implementation complete.** The URL shortener API is built with ASP.NET Core 8 minimal APIs + EF Core 8/Npgsql:\n\n- **`POST /links`** — validates URL (absolute http/https with host) and optional custom code (`^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`), returns 201 `{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}` with the URL unchanged, generates an 8-char unique code when omitted, 409 on duplicate custom code, 422 on bad input including malformed JSON (parsed manually so `JsonException` maps to 422, not 400).\n- **`GET /links/{code}`** — 200 or 404 with `{\"error\":...}`; **`GET /r/{code}`** — 302 with byte-exact `Location`, atomic `ExecuteUpdate` increment (exactly once, no lost updates); **`GET /links`** — ascending creation order by identity PK with `total`.\n- **Persistence** — PostgreSQL connection parsed from `DATABASE_URL` (no hard-coded credentials), `Migrations/` applied on startup; data and click counts verified to survive restarts, and a dropped-DB cold start re-migrates cleanly.\n- **`start.sh`** — applies pending migrations (`--migrate-only` pass, plus idempotent migrate-at-startup) then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` from the pre-published Release build; dependencies were installed during development, not at start time.\n- **README.md** documents the start procedure, API surface, and rules.\n\nMy 56-assertion test battery passed (the one \"failure\" was a bug in the test script itself, re-verified separately), and all test servers were stopped afterward."
